    "text": "The program is a lazy greedy heuristic and was not compiled or run on any data set.\n\n1. A BFS over all cells (8 neighbours, walls included) from the initial backbone cell gives a parent pointer and distance for every cell. Connecting a router means walking up the parent pointers until a connected cell is reached. The union of these paths forms a tree, so the connected cells can be output in order of BFS distance (parents before children).\n2. Every non-wall, reachable cell is a router candidate. Its coverage is computed per quadrant with a small DP: a cell is covered if the cell before it in the row and the cell before it in the column are both covered, and the cell itself is not a wall.\n3. A priority queue holds candidates keyed by uncovered target cells gained \u00d7 1000 divided by (Pr + Pb \u00d7 new backbone cells needed). Keys are refreshed lazily when a candidate is popped. An unaffordable candidate is discarded, and a candidate with zero gain is skipped.\n4. A cap on the number of evaluations keeps the run deterministic and within the time limit, instead of a timer.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint H,W,R;\nvector<string> g;\nvector<char> cov,conn;\nstatic int dxs[8]={-1,-1,-1,0,0,1,1,1},dys[8]={-1,0,1,-1,1,-1,0,1};\nint gainOf(int r,int c,bool mark){\n    int cnt=0;\n    bool ok[11][11];\n    for(int sx=-1;sx<=1;sx+=2)for(int sy=-1;sy<=1;sy+=2){\n        for(int dx=0;dx<=R;dx++)for(int dy=0;dy<=R;dy++){\n            int x=r+sx*dx,y=c+sy*dy;\n            bool o;\n            if(x<0||y<0||x>=H||y>=W||g[x][y]=='#')o=false;\n            else o=(dx==0||ok[dx-1][dy])&&(dy==0||ok[dx][dy-1]);\n            ok[dx][dy]=o;\n            if(o&&(sx==1||dx>0)&&(sy==1||dy>0)&&g[x][y]=='.'&&!cov[x*W+y]){\n                cnt++;\n                if(mark)cov[x*W+y]=1;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return cnt;\n}\nint main(){\n    long long Pb,Pr,B;int br,bc;\n    cin>>H>>W>>R>>Pb>>Pr>>B>>br>>bc;\n    g.resize(H);\n    for(auto&s:g)cin>>s;\n    int n=H*W;\n    vector<int> par(n,-1),dist(n,-1);\n    vector<int> q;q.reserve(n);\n    int root=br*W+bc;\n    dist[root]=0;q.push_back(root);\n    for(size_t i=0;i<q.size();i++){\n        int u=q[i];int r=u/W,c=u%W;\n        for(int k=0;k<8;k++){\n            int x=r+dxs[k],y=c+dys[k];\n            if(x<0||y<0||x>=H||y>=W)continue;\n            int v=x*W+y;\n            if(dist[v]>=0)continue;\n            dist[v]=dist[u]+1;par[v]=u;q.push_back(v);\n        }\n    }\n    cov.assign(n,0);conn.assign(n,0);\n    conn[root]=1;\n    auto marg=[&](int v){\n        int m=0;\n        while(!conn[v]){m++;v=par[v];}\n        return m;\n    };\n    typedef pair<double,int> P;\n    priority_queue<P> pq;\n    for(int v=0;v<n;v++){\n        if(dist[v]<0||g[v/W][v%W]=='#')continue;\n        int gn=gainOf(v/W,v%W,false);\n        if(gn<=0)continue;\n        double key=gn*1000.0/(Pr+Pb*(double)dist[v]);\n        pq.push({key,v});\n    }\n    long long spent=0;\n    vector<int> routers,cells;\n    long long evals=0;\n    while(!pq.empty()&&evals<4000000){\n        auto [k,v]=pq.top();pq.pop();\n        evals++;\n        int m=marg(v);\n        long long cost=Pr+Pb*(long long)m;\n        if(spent+cost>B)continue;\n        int gn=gainOf(v/W,v%W,false);\n        if(gn<=0)continue;\n        double key=gn*1000.0/cost;\n        if(!pq.empty()&&key<pq.top().first){pq.push({key,v});continue;}\n        gainOf(v/W,v%W,true);\n        int u=v;\n        while(!conn[u]){conn[u]=1;cells.push_back(u);u=par[u];}\n        spent+=cost;\n        routers.push_back(v);\n    }\n    sort(cells.begin(),cells.end(),[&](int a,int b){\n        if(dist[a]!=dist[b])return dist[a]<dist[b];\n        return a<b;});\n    string out=to_string(cells.size())+\"\\n\";\n    for(int v:cells)out+=to_string(v/W)+\" \"+to_string(v%W)+\"\\n\";\n    out+=to_string(routers.size())+\"\\n\";\n    for(int v:routers)out+=to_string(v/W)+\" \"+to_string(v%W)+\"\\n\";\n    fputs(out.c_str(),stdout);\n}\n```",
